hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27287","Hajjaj narrated to us, and Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, they said: Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, and Ishaq ibn Sulayman said: I heard Ibn Abi Dhib, from Salih, the freed slave of al-Tawamah, from Abi Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to his wives in the year of the Farewell Hajj: This, then the backs of mats. He said: They all used to perform Hajj except Zaynab daughter of Jahsh and Sawdah daughter of Zamah, and they both would say: By Allah, no mount shall move us after we heard that from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Ishaq ibn Sulayman said in his hadith: They said: By Allah, no mount shall move us after the statement of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: This, then the backs of mats. And Yazid said: After we heard that from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"27288","Hammad ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah, meaning Ibn Umar, narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Zaynab daughter of Jahsh, that she used to comb the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and she said once: I used to comb the head of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in a basin of brass."
"27289","Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, he said: al-Darawardi narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Umar informed me, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Zaynab daughter of Jahsh, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to perform ablution in a basin of brass."
"27290","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Malik informed us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from Humayd ibn Nafi, that Zaynab daughter of Abi Salamah informed him, that she entered upon Zaynab daughter of Jahsh, wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, upon the minbar saying: It is not lawful for a woman believing in Allah and the Last Day to mourn over a dead above three nights, except over a husband, four months and ten."
